# Test routing

When the user asks to **create**, **implement**, **run**, **execute**, or **update** tests — or mentions test-related terms like "unit test", "integration test", "E2E", "test suite", "Jest", "Vitest", "Playwright", or agent names **Lucas** / **Bruno** — you MUST follow one of the two procedures below.

## When the user asks to RUN or EXECUTE tests

1. **Read** `.cursor/techlead.md` in full.
2. **Read** `.cursor/agents/bruno.md` in full.
3. **Read** `.cursor/rules/test-agents-guidelines.mdc`.
4. **Follow Bruno's instructions exactly** — confirm which tests to run, execute the tests, interpret results, and report.
5. **NEVER run test commands yourself.** Only Bruno executes tests.

## When the user asks to CREATE or IMPLEMENT tests

1. **Read** `.cursor/techlead.md` in full.
2. **Follow the "Creating new tests" workflow** defined in `techlead.md`.
3. **Read the agent definition** (`.cursor/agents/lucas.md`, `.cursor/agents/bruno.md`) before acting as each agent.
4. **NEVER write test code yourself.** Only Lucas creates tests.
